          "thm-refined-campbell-formula-and-palm-law-existence",
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-countable-choice"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "statement": "Under the pair-correlation density hypothesis, K(r)=integral_{B[0,r]} g(u) du for every r>=0. If eta is simple, K(r)=rho^{-1}E^0[mu(B[0,r]\\{0})].",
        "strategy": "Substitute the reduced Palm identity into the K definition, then use the density formula; in the simple case Palm configurations have exactly one origin occurrence.",
