        "justified_by": [],
        "statement": "For U uniform on [0,1), eta_U=sum_{k in Z}delta_{k+U} is a stationary simple point process of intensity 1. Its full Palm law is the unit lattice sum_{k in Z}delta_k, and alpha_red^(2) has unit atoms at nonzero integers, so no pair-correlation density exists. For the multiplicity-bearing process 2 eta_U, the Palm configuration has multiplicity 2 at every lattice site; deleting one distinguished origin occurrence leaves one at zero, alpha_red^(2)({0})=2, and K(0)=1/2.",
        "strategy": "Finite window and lattice sums are evaluated explicitly; stationarity, Palm law, atomic reduced measure, and K(0) are each verified.",
